00:03:10.130 --> 00:03:13.550
There are a lot of model
formats in TensorFlow.

00:03:13.550 --> 00:03:16.640
In its short life, it's
managed to accumulate several.

00:03:16.640 --> 00:03:22.850
And this area of serving
TensorFlow models

00:03:22.850 --> 00:03:25.190
involves having some
deeper knowledge

00:03:25.190 --> 00:03:29.270
about what those model
formats are, how, ultimately,

00:03:29.270 --> 00:03:33.230
to load them using code
and operate on them,

00:03:33.230 --> 00:03:35.660
and so on, and transform them.

00:03:35.660 --> 00:03:38.360
We'll talk about
optimization tools that

00:03:38.360 --> 00:03:40.760
are useful for this purpose.

00:03:40.760 --> 00:03:44.020
There are several tools
present in the TensorFlow code

00:03:44.020 --> 00:03:48.470
base that can be used to
optimize TensorFlow models.

00:03:48.470 --> 00:03:51.800
There are also
facilities or tools

00:03:51.800 --> 00:03:54.500
to optimize TensorFlow that
are built into the TensorFlow

00:03:54.500 --> 00:03:56.380
runtime as well.

00:03:56.380 --> 00:03:59.450
Matter of fact, much of what
